    "q-44989": {
      "dom_id": "step-q44989",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The formula for the $n$th term of an geometric sequence is ${a}_{n}=0.1\\cdot {2}^{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$  What is the recursive formula for this sequence?",
      "worked_solution": "The recursive formula for an geometric sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we must determine the common ratio $r$ and state the first term ${a}_{1}.$ The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =0.1\\cdot {2}^{1}=0.2, \\\\ {a}_{2} & =0.1\\cdot {2}^{2}=0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{0.4}{0.2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula for the geometric  sequence is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n+1} & =2{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=0.2,\\,n\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
